    "items": [
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Song or Psalm of Asaph."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Keep not thou silence, O God:",
          "Hold not thy peace, and be not still, O God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For, lo, thine enemies make a tumult:",
          "And they that hate thee have lifted up the head."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They have taken crafty counsel against thy people,",
          "And consulted against thy hidden ones."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They have said, Come, and let us cut them off from being a nation;",
          "That the name of Israel may be no more in remembrance."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For they have consulted together with one consent:",
          "They are confederate against thee:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The tabernacles of Edom, and the Ishmaelites;",
          "Of Moab, and the Hagarenes;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Gebal, and Ammon, and Amalek;",
          "The Philistines with the inhabitants of Tyre;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Assur also is joined with them:",
          "They have holpen the children of Lot."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do unto them as unto the Midianites;",
          "As to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the brook of Kison:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Which perished at Endor:",
          "They became as dung for the earth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Make their nobles like Oreb, and like Zeeb:",
          "Yea, all their princes as Zebah, and as Zalmunna:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who said, Let us take to ourselves",
          "The houses of God in possession."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "O my God, make them like a wheel;",
          "As the stubble before the wind."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "As the fire burneth a wood,",
          "And as the flame setteth the mountains on fire;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "So persecute them with thy tempest,",
          "And make them afraid with thy storm."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Fill their faces with shame;",
          "That they may seek thy name, O LORD."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Let them be confounded and troubled for ever;",
          "Yea, let them be put to shame, and perish:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "That men may know that thou, whose name alone is JEHOVAH,",
          "Art the Most High over all the earth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
